# Mexican Sushi Bowl

A deconstructed approach inspired by Mexico City’s fusion sushi scene

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

- [ ] [Smoked salmon]{ ing="smoked-salmon" }, sliced
- [ ] [Sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" }
- [ ] [Black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, cooked
- [ ] [Corn kernels]{ ing="corn-kernels" } (fresh, frozen, or grilled)
- [ ] [Avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, diced or sliced
- [ ] [Pico de gallo]{ ing="pico-de-gallo" } or salsa
- [ ] [Pickled jalapeño slices]{ ing="pickled-jalapeno-slices" }
- [ ] [Cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, diced
- [ ] [Radishes]{ ing="radishes" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] [Cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, fresh
- [ ] [Queso fresco]{ ing="queso-fresco" }, crumbled
- [ ] [Lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }

### Chipotle-Avocado Dressing

- [ ] 1 [ripe avocado]{ ing="ripe-avocado" }
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [lime juice]{ ing="lime-juice" }
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [chipotle powder]{ ing="chipotle-powder" } or chipotle in adobo
- [ ] 1 clove [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste
- [ ] 2-3 Tbsp [water]{ ing="water" } to thin

## Recipe

1. Prepare [sushi rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } and let cool
1. Make the chipotle-[avocado]{ ing="avocado" } dressing by blending all ingredients until smooth
1. Arrange [rice]{ ing="sushi-rice" } in bowls
1. Top with [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, corn, [cucumber]{ ing="cucumber" }, [radishes]{ ing="radishes" }
1. Add [smoked salmon]{ ing="smoked-salmon" }, [avocado]{ ing="avocado" }, and [pico de gallo]{ ing="pico-de-gallo" }
1. Garnish with pickled jalapeños, fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, and [queso fresco]{ ing="queso-fresco" }
1. Drizzle with chipotle-[avocado]{ ing="avocado" } dressing
1. Serve with [lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }

## Notes

1. This bowl captures Mexico City’s love for mixing Japanese and Mexican flavors
1. Black beans and corn add authentic Mexican elements
1. Chipotle-avocado dressing replaces cream cheese-based sauces
1. The combination is fresh, spicy, and satisfying
1. Queso fresco adds a salty, creamy element without being heavy
1. Great for meal prep - keep components separate and assemble when ready to eat
1. Can use any salsa you prefer - mild to spicy based on your taste
